  "design": {
    "decision": "Buy [♦] honors and later synthetic [♦] honors over other cards, and keep them out of Opening swaps and conversions that would give them away. The points are lost on a set, so the team still has to bid the honors' tricks accurately.",
    "opponent": "Revealed at the start of play. Opponents expect [♦] honors from this team and void [♦] to trump them.",
    "rationale": "The brief asks for [♦] holding pieces. This one gives the honors line its Hold trigger, so the honors line now pays on Hold, Lead and Win alike, as the archetype tables intend. It mirrors the kept ca-high-spade-hold at uncommon strength for the side suit, using the standard honors range. A team holds about two [♦] honors, so it is roughly 80 points before any shop investment.",
